# ToupTek / OMAX USB cameras. The vendor ids are the two that the ToupTek SDK's own rule lists (0x0547 and 0x04b4).
#
# The SDK's rule makes these devices writable by every user (MODE="0666"). This rule grants access instead to
#   - whoever is logged in at the computer's own screen and keyboard (TAG+="uaccess"), and
#   - members of the group plugdev (MODE="0660", GROUP="plugdev"): that covers a login over SSH, and the first user of Raspberry Pi OS
#     is normally in plugdev (check with the command `groups`).
#
# The file name starts with 70 on purpose: uaccess only works from a rule that runs before 73-seat-late.rules.
#
# Install: sudo install -m 644 70-toupcam.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/ && sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger
# and unplug and re-plug the camera. `scripts/install_toupcam.py --udev` and `packaging/install_pi.sh` do this for you, and remove the
# older, world-writable 99-toupcam.rules that earlier installs left behind.
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="0547", MODE="0660", GROUP="plugdev", TAG+="uaccess"
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="04b4", MODE="0660", GROUP="plugdev", TAG+="uaccess"
